.TH std::basic_spanbuf 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::basic_spanbuf \- std::basic_spanbuf

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <spanstream>
template<

class CharT,
class Traits = std::char_traits<CharT>        (since C++23)
> class basic_spanbuf

: public std::basic_streambuf<CharT, Traits>

std::basic_spanbuf is a std::basic_streambuf whose associated character sequence is a
memory-resident sequence of arbitrary characters, which can be initialized from or made
available as an instance of std::span<CharT>.

std::basic_spanbuf performs I/O on a fixed buffer, and therefore it does not attempt to
obtain a new buffer when the underlying buffer is exhausted.

Several typedefs for common character types are provided:

Defined in header <spanstream>
